{
  "an4.45:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 4.45 ",
  "an4.45:0.2": "5. With Rohitassa ",
  "an4.45:0.3": "With Rohitassa ",
  "an4.45:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "an4.45:1.2": "Then, late at night, the glorious godling Rohitassa, lighting up the entire Jeta’s Grove, went up to the Buddha, bowed, stood to one side, and said to him: ",
  "an4.45:2.1": "“Sir, is it possible to know or see or reach the end of the world by traveling to a place where there’s no being born, growing old, dying, passing away, or being reborn?” ",
  "an4.45:2.2": "“Reverend, I say it’s not possible to know or see or reach the end of the world by traveling to a place where there’s no being born, growing old, dying, passing away, or being reborn.” ",
  "an4.45:3.1": "“It’s incredible, sir, it’s amazing, ",
  "an4.45:3.2": "how well said this was by the Buddha. ",
  "an4.45:3.3": "",
  "an4.45:4.1": "Once upon a time, I was a seer named Rohitassa, son of the benefactors. I was a sky-walker with psychic powers. ",
  "an4.45:4.2": "I was as fast as a light arrow easily shot across the shadow of a palm tree by a well-trained expert archer with a strong bow. ",
  "an4.45:4.3": "My stride was such that it could span from the eastern ocean to the western ocean. ",
  "an4.45:4.4": "Having such speed and stride, this wish came to me: ",
  "an4.45:4.5": "‘I will reach the end of the world by traveling.’ ",
  "an4.45:4.6": "I traveled for my 